A||||4||dupi||need help, 86 GT will not start!!!!!!!!
Z||000000||dupi||08-30-99||03:36 PM||||The first problem with this car was while driving on the highway with my foot on gas the motor just cut off and afterwards wouldn't start. After that I discovered a cracked battery and replaced it,also replaced the pick-up coil,ignition switch.I recently did a tune up and replaced the cap,rotor,coil,plugs and wires, but the car will not start and is also not getting any spark. Also it's a V-6,just in case.Any help would be greatly appreciated.<p>       Thanks, Joe
Z||000001||dupi||08-30-99||03:40 PM||||P.S. I forgot to add that I checked all grounds coming off the battery and from the block to the frame and all fusible links for continunity.
Z||000002||DJRice||08-31-99||07:36 AM||||Are you getting any juice to the car at all.  Dash lighting up?  You may want to replace battery cables....Also check the fusible links.  Make sure the connections are tight at the distribution block below the main engine harness near the battery.
Z||000003||ChadMan||08-31-99||08:37 AM||||I bet it's a fusible link.  My 84 Coupe once left me stranded four miles from home in late December, in a snowstorm.  By the time I walked home, I swore I'd sell that little plastic piece of crap.  $105 later ($45 of which was towing) I was back in business and in love with my Fiero again.  Good luck.
Z||000004||ka4nkf||08-31-99||03:31 PM||||There Is A Pigtale Connector In The Wiring Harness By The Battery. Make Sure This Is Connected, It Controls The Memory To The ECM.
